Syriac and Arabic, “of Ramim.” (Calmet) — The ox. Protestants, “the oxen stumbled.”"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Divided. Slain. See chap. xiv. 11., 1 Kings xv. 32., and 2 Kings vi. 7. (Haydock) — The soul of brutes perishes; that of man is only divided from the body by death."],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Obededom. A Levite was judged more proper to guard the ark, chap. xv. 18. — Gethite. Because he had dwelt in Geth. (Worthington)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}